{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511080-practical-suggestions-for-improving-representation","id":1511080,"title":"Practical suggestions for improving representation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-08T11:41:46-07:00","id":1511080,"title":"Practical suggestions for improving representation","content":"So I have no interest in playing 5th edition Werewolf but I have been follwoing their efforts to improve the representation of indigenous cultures. While it is clearly a work in progress, I appreciate that they have made an effort to consult with folks with relevant experiences and cultural ties.<br /> <br /> I would love to complie some practical suggestions on how to improve this and other cultural representation in 20th anniversary games.<br /> <br /> So far I have changed the tribe names for younger and older brother/sibling to the 5e versions while generally keeping the lore. However, I have made it explicit that while Werewolf tribes may exist adjacent to different cultures they are not representative of them. Instead, it is my cannon that the Garou have always been a secret known to select humans, but that the course of the many communities in North and South America was never directed by any supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> I have been doing research and reading to understand what cultural elements are reasonable to include in a game and which should be avoided.<br /> <br /> I have asked all players to carefully consider how they are portraying characters with a different culture than their own.<br /> <br /> I am committing to pay people from relevant communities for artwork depicting indigenous elements vs randomly selecting items from the internet that may not even depict the culture or people in question.<br /> <br /> <br /> One item that is still very much an open question for me are Metis. Some kind of name change is easy, but I feel like their existence is pretty central to the game. I have always tried to emphasize that while prejudice exists among Garou , that all werewolves born in this way are still full individuals with the capacity to be as heroic or villainous as anyone else. Still, it is a messy element.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3344-thelongnight","user":"TheLongNight","date":". 05-09-2023, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3344-thelongnight","name":"TheLongNight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3344_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T11:58:41-07:00","id":1511081,"title":"","content":"Just from my side as a non-American white person, but the best way to avoid the 'member of the tribe must be X ethnicity'-issue is to treat the garou of that tribe living in the US as different from those who live in their homelands. Because I feel the assumption that comes from seeing the tribes found in the US (and since the games were originally made with only US people in mind) as the same as in their homelands creates this sense of insularity that shouldn't be there.<br /> <br /> Second, about the garou born. The thing with them is that OOCly they are a bit of a hard thing to deal with for other players, as some are not comfortable playing out ableism and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T14:08:34-07:00","id":1511082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheLongNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511080-practical-suggestions-for-improving-representation#post1511080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One item that is still very much an open question for me are Metis. Some kind of name change is easy, but I feel like their existence is pretty central to the game. I have always tried to emphasize that while prejudice exists among Garou , that all werewolves born in this way are still full individuals with the capacity to be as heroic or villainous as anyone else. Still, it is a messy element.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean messy element?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T14:49:41-07:00","id":1511086,"title":"","content":"The Garou are supernatural creatures and not humans. The tribes are cults devoted to their tribal Incarna. Human cultures only influence the homid members of the tribe and their kinfolk. They should be mostly immaterial to lupus and metis except by proxy. And in a long enough time period, the human cultures of their human kinfolk change, but the actual tribal culture - based on devotion to the tribal incarna - should be fairly intact and have continuity.<br /> <br /> So you only need to think more about what should be the (fictional) Garou culture - based around devotion to the tribal incarna, not about real world human culture that its homid members are brought up in.<br /> <br /> The human culture of a tribe's homid members have a place in their identity, and of course is very important to whatever community their kinfolk belong to. But this is an easy element to deal with IMO. It's just that is easier (more lazy) to rely on the homid ancestry of a tribe to develop it (in terms of culture, history, lore, etc.), rather than invent original concepts around each tribe's incarna and spirit brood, so that is what's too often been done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T22:11:29-07:00","id":1511104,"title":"","content":"Better to cut any ethnograpchic-cultural-religious ties, that could be compromised. Garou shoud have their own (sub)culture - like Uratha - anything else is up to players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}